---
import Layout from "../components/Layout.astro";
import CommandBlock from "../components/CommandBlock.astro";
import SafetyNotice from "../components/SafetyNotice.astro";
---

<Layout title="ArkheionX Examples" description="Public-safe local fixtures and example review workflows for ArkheionX.">
  <header class="page-intro page-shell">
    <p class="page-kicker">Controlled inputs</p>
    <h1>Examples built for inspection.</h1>
    <p>Every example on this page is a toy or local fixture. It demonstrates artifact shape and workflow, not a real protocol finding.</p>
  </header>

  <div class="page-shell">
    <section class="prose-section">
      <h2>Bundled demo workflow</h2>
      <p>List the bundled demos, inspect one, then copy it to a disposable directory.</p>
      <CommandBlock
        command={`arkheionx demo --list
arkheionx demo --show oracle-staking
arkheionx demo --copy oracle-staking /tmp/arkheionx-demo
arkheionx review-map /tmp/arkheionx-demo`}
      />
    </section>

    <section class="prose-section">
      <h2>Public fixture surfaces</h2>
      <div class="definition-grid">
        <div><dt>Oracle staking</dt><dd>A small staking and reward shape with an oracle dependency for mapping roles and assumptions.</dd></div>
        <div><dt>AMM / lending hybrid</dt><dd>A local composite shape for examining cross-component value paths and accounting boundaries.</dd></div>
        <div><dt>Mini vault</dt><dd>A compact vault surface suitable for the first scan and review-map commands.</dd></div>
        <div><dt>Fixture harness sets</dt><dd>Nine static Solidity-like inputs used to check deterministic IDs, fingerprints, and snapshots.</dd></div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="prose-section">
      <h2>Generate a review package</h2>
      <p>Artifacts stay under the selected repository's <code>.arkheionx/out/</code> directory.</p>
      <CommandBlock
        command={`arkheionx scan /tmp/arkheionx-demo
arkheionx review-map /tmp/arkheionx-demo
arkheionx review-package /tmp/arkheionx-demo --strict`}
      />
      <p>Open the manifest and review-map files directly. Treat every machine-produced signal as a lead to inspect against source.</p>
    </section>

    <SafetyNotice title="Example boundary" />
  </div>
</Layout>
